# ... but VENDORED TEST FIXTURES must be committed (2026-07-11).
#
# The blanket `*.cif` above exists to keep the 8.77 GB / 18,079-file AlphaFold structure
# cache (data/raw/cache/alphafold/) out of the repository -- and it should. But it also
# silently swallowed tests/fixtures/alphafold/AF-E7ENB7-F1-model_v4.cif, the 101 KB
# structure the AlphaFold feature tests need.
#
# That mattered: `git add` on an ignored path does NOTHING and says NOTHING. The fixture
# would never have reached Continuous Integration, and the seven tests that validate
# pLDDT (predicted Local Distance Difference Test) parsing, RSA (Relative Solvent
# Accessibility), DSSP (Define Secondary Structure of Proteins) records, alpha-carbon
# geometry and the residue off-by-one tripwire would have gone on skipping there -- the
# exact defect the fixture was vendored to fix, reintroduced invisibly by a .gitignore line.
#
# Negations MUST come after the rule they override. Precedent: `!tests/fixtures/*.parquet`
# (line ~64), which covers only the top level -- this one recurses.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.cif

